<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carnuntum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carnuntum was a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress and town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Bratislava</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>. Capital of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> Superior, it lay on the Amber Road and was a base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcomannic-wars">Marcomannic Wars</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> was proclaimed emperor there in 193, and an imperial conference met there in 308.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carnuntum.jpg" alt="Carnuntum" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archaeotux at German Wikipedia (Original text: archaeotux) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carnuntum_map_Roman_city.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
